I consider it valid to 'E'ngrave your pack contents in the dust when you
get hit by amnesia.  When I see that 'E'ngraving, I use it as a note to see
what the player was carring when he was killed.  (I don't do it normally
because it takes time.)  The side effect is that these engravings will
remind your future characters of what you are carrying, and will tell other
players as well.  

This is really more of a gray area of Nethack tactics - as is writing
"Closed for Inventory" infront of every single locked door. 

If it really is a problem, all the devteam has to do is to randomly adjust
some of the dropped items (e.g. sometimes swapping a wand of death with a
wand of haste monster.)

